Subject: [PATCH] feat(glm5_next): SGL_PROBE_MOE=dense, the routed experts without EPMoE's dispatch

GLM-5.3-Flash's first capture check on a v5p-64 at --tp-size 32
--ep-size 32 (2026-09-27) passed its first three layers at 0.98 to 1.10
times transformers' own BF16 error and jumped to 2.6 at the slot after
layer 3, its first MoE layer. Nemotron 3 Ultra showed the same jump after
its MoE layers, and the switches that swap the top-k, the gmm kernel, the
router and the latent projections there didn't move it. That left EPMoE's
dispatch in the routed path: the sort by expert, the group sizes, the
padding, and the unpermute with the top-k weights, which this model also
casts to BF16 before the experts. The jump came from the CPU reference,
which rounded the float32 router bias to BF16, and against the rebuilt
reference every layer passed on 2026-09-28 (models/glm5.3-flash.md).

SGL_PROBE_MOE=dense, read when the model traces, replaces
Glm5NextEPMoE._forward's body with layers/moe_probe.py's dense_experts:
every local expert runs over every token in float32 at HIGHEST with the
clamped SwiGLU, each token's row scales by its float32 top-k weight for
that expert (zero when it didn't pick it), and the shard's sum goes
through EPMoE's own reduce over the tensor and expert axes in float32.
Glm5NextMoE hands the experts float32 weights under the switch. Off by
default, and a run without it traces the program the model patch traced.
layers/moe_probe.py is the file nemotron3-probe.patch adds; this model
reads only SGL_PROBE_MOE and logs it when it's on.
---
 python/sgl_jax/srt/layers/moe_probe.py | 226 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 python/sgl_jax/srt/models/glm5_next.py |  34 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 259 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

